ktitle":"Proc. IEEE Automatic Speech Recognition and Understanding Workshop","year":"2011","month":"December","abstract":"We review developments in the SRI Language Modeling Toolkit (SRILM) since 2002, when a previous paper on SRILM was published. These developments include measures to make training from large data sets more efficient, to implement additional language modeling techniques (such as for adaptation and smoothing), and for client/server operation. In addition, the functionality for lattice processing has been greatly expanded. We also highlight several external contributions and notable applications of the toolkit, and assess SRILM’s impact on the research community.","publisher":"IEEE SPS","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/publication/srilm-at-sixteen-update-and-outlook/","edition":"Proc. IEEE Automatic Speech Recognition and Understanding Workshop"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"streamingrnnt","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:30:07Z","response_hash":"b1dba319ed5a7684","fields":{"author":"He, Yanzhang and Sainath, Tara N. and Prabhavalkar, Rohit and McGraw, Ian and Alvarez, Raziel and Zhao, Ding and Rybach, David and Kannan, Anjuli and Wu, Yonghui and Pang, Ruoming and Liang, Qiao and Bhatia, Deepti and Shangguan, Yuan and Li, Bo and Pundak, Golan and Sim, Khe Chai and Bagby, Tom and Chang, Shuo-yiin and Rao, Kanishka and Gruenstein, Alexander","booktitle":"Proc. ICASSP","title":"Streaming End-to-end Speech Recognition for Mobile Devices","year":"2019","volume":"","number":"","pages":"6381-6385","doi":"10.1109/ICASSP.2019.8682336"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"teacherstudent1","verdict":"verified","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:30:07Z","response_hash":"5227688ec959ea9a","fields":{"title":"Sequence Student-Teacher Training of De